# metric-autopsy probes — git 28974ab, python 3.13.16, numpy 2.5.3
=================== p01_null_metrics_and_offset.py
P1a: constant metric lambda d: 0.0 on clean data, via run_autopsy defaults
  G0 PASS     expectation stable under all nuisance perturbations (no shift beyond estimator noise)
  G1 PASS     all 2 strata within 1.5x QC (worst 1.00x)
  G2 FAIL     effect collapses under matching: 0 -> 0 (0% retained, need >= 50%) — likely a QC artifact
  VERDICT: FAIL — died at GATE 2 (n_genes matching)

P1b: random-number metric (pure noise, no data dependence)
  G0 PASS     expectation stable under all nuisance perturbations (no shift beyond estimator noise)
  G1 PASS     all 2 strata within 1.5x QC (worst 1.00x)
  G2 PASS     no meaningful pre-matching effect (|-0.08415| < null floor 1.915) — nothing to preserve; the groups simply do not differ on this metric
  VERDICT: PASS — cleared 3 auto gates; treat as provisional until replicated

P1c: GATE 0 location-invariance: mi_3bin vs mi_3bin + C on clean data
  C=    0: GATE0 FAIL  worst=extra_dropout rel=0.619 z=27.9
  C=  0.5: GATE0 PASS  worst=extra_dropout rel=0.105 z=27.9
  C=    1: GATE0 PASS  worst=extra_dropout rel=0.057 z=27.9
  C=   10: GATE0 PASS  worst=extra_dropout rel=0.006 z=27.9

P1d: GATE 0 scale-invariance? mi_3bin * k
  k=     1: GATE0 FAIL
  k=   100: GATE0 FAIL
  k=  0.01: GATE0 FAIL

P1e: affine reparametrisation of norm_pearson: Fisher z / (1 - r)
  r                           : GATE0 PASS worst=depth_downsample rel=0.048 base=0.520
  1-r (a 'decoupling' score)  : GATE0 PASS worst=depth_downsample rel=0.052 base=0.480
  atanh(r)                    : GATE0 PASS worst=depth_downsample rel=0.059 base=0.577
