=================== p04_xist_same_data_control.py
metric = mean log1p(CP10k) of Xist; group_col=sex (female vs male); within=['age']
  G0 PASS     expectation stable under all nuisance perturbations (no shift beyond estimator noise)
  G1 FAIL     1/2 strata fail QC parity: 1 exceed 1.5x QC ratio (worst 2.00x at {'age': 'old'}); 1 have n_genes overlap < 0.2 (worst 0.00 at {'age': 'old'}) — unusa
  G2 PASS     effect survives matching: 7.731 -> 7.751 (100% retained, subset balanced 1.00x)
  VERDICT: FAIL — died at GATE 1 (QC parity)

per-stratum QC table from GATE 1:
   {'age': 'old'} median n_genes female=32 male=16 ratio=2.00 overlap=0.00 flagged=True
   {'age': 'young'} median n_genes female=32 male=31 ratio=1.03 overlap=0.86 flagged=False

Arithmetic on the manuscript's real TMS table (§4): old stratum female/male = 3413/1701 = 2.01x > 1.5x
